cmocean
-------

This repository bundles cmocean-style colormap data under:

    assets/colormaps/cmocean/

cmocean is a collection of perceptually uniform colormaps for oceanography and
related scientific visualization. The MATLAB cmocean package is associated with
Kristen M. Thyng and Chad A. Greene, with additional authorship/citation
information in the cmocean project documentation:

    https://github.com/chadagreene/cmocean
    https://github.com/matplotlib/cmocean

If these colormaps are useful in scientific work, please consider citing:

    Thyng, K.M., C.A. Greene, R.D. Hetland, H.M. Zimmerle, and S.F. DiMarco.
    2016. True colors of oceanography: Guidelines for effective and accurate
    colormap selection. Oceanography 29(3):9-13.
    https://dx.doi.org/10.5670/oceanog.2016.66

cmocean is distributed under an MIT-style license in its upstream packages.


Scientific colour maps by Fabio Crameri
---------------------------------------

This repository bundles Scientific colour map data under:

    assets/colormaps/Crameri/

These colour maps are developed by Fabio Crameri and collaborators for
accurate, colour-blind-friendly scientific visualization:

    https://www.fabiocrameri.ch/colourmaps/
    https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1243862

If these colormaps are useful in scientific work, please cite the upstream
Scientific colour maps publication/version as appropriate. Common citations
include:

    Crameri, F. (2018). Scientific colour maps. Zenodo.
    https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1243862

    Crameri, F., Shephard, G.E., and Heron, P.J. (2020). The misuse of colour
    in science communication. Nature Communications, 11, 5444.
    https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-020-19160-7


